-- Concrete separation (Carson et al. 2003 reduced latent inhibition; Carhart-Harris REBUS):
-- Rigid prior admits only `false` (conventional category); relaxed prior admits both `Bool`.
-- The novel insight `true` is excluded under the rigid prior yet inhabited under the relaxed prior.
rigid-blocks-novel : Neg ((h : Bool) × (h ≡ false) × (h ≡ true))
rigid-blocks-novel w = true≢false (concat (sym (snd (snd w))) (fst (snd w)))
